I just had a perfect nightmare scenario happen to me in a local game of
Nethack.  I was walking through Minetown burdened, lugging some stuff
to a store, when an arch-lich appears next to me.  Obviously a
chameleon, out to make trouble and now an incredibly serious threat.
The scenario as it played out was a mixture of both good and bad luck
that is so particularly Nethack.

- I had no wands of fire, lightning, or digging, so I couldn't carve an
Elbereth.
- I had no scrolls of scare monster.
- I had no MR or cold resistance.  I did have reflection (from
Sokoban).
- I was normal speed, not fast, and burdened.

The arch-lich popped next to me, and cast its freezing touch spell,
halving my HP.  Since I was burdened, it got a double turn and used it
to summon an Olog-Hai next to me.  I had roughly 50 hp, and -7 ac, so
this Olog-Hai was also a very serious threat.  Naturally my biggest
fear was the Touch of Death, and I had no potions of hallucination or
MR.  Now my turn came up, and I took a small break from the game before
considering my options.  After poring over my inventory screen a few
times, I realized the situation was pretty dire, for the reasons stated
above.  I finally decided to try dusting an Elbereth; I didn't see much
other choice.  Dropping stuff to unburden myself would have given my
enemies a free turn.

The dusted Elbereth didn't work.  After this streak of incredibly bad
luck, here came the good luck.  The Olog-Hai zapped a wand of death at
me!  It reflected from my medallion, and killed him.  The chameleon
also decided to turn into a gremlin, which I quickly dispatched.  Whew!

Postmortem:  The only other viable move I had available to me, as far
as I know, would have been to try to put the Olog-Hai to sleep with my
wand (I was a Gnomish healer).  I would have had to take my chances
with the Touch of Death and the chameleon in any case.  Also, I'm not
in the habit of being encumbered except for very short stretches, and
this was a typical example of why I sometimes choose to do so:  lugging
equipment to a shop.  I doubt this encounter will change that habit.
This has also reaffirmed my high estimation for the ring of protection
from shape changers.

This encounter raised a couple of questions for me, that I did a little
sourcediving to answer:

- Does your encumbrance affect the chance of dusting an Elbereth?  I
checked engrave.c, and saw no reference to 'encumber' or 'capacity',
save the check to see if you're overtaxed (which prevents you from
engraving at all).  The if-statement that checks to see whether a
letter should be corrupted didn't check for encumbrance, nor the
player's luck.
- Does player luck affect the chance of the Touch of Death working?
Sadly, no.  The Touch of Death doesn't always work -- it's based on the
caster's level.

This raises a new question for me:
- Does the shape-changer also assume the level of the mimicked monster?
 I haven't looked into this one yet.



